# Elevation

The elevation analyzers (the ELEV rules) over the F# product projects of
`Berreman/Berreman.slnx`, run by `Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1`. The rules
are STL's `Softellect.Analyzers` package, at the version the root
`Directory.Build.targets` pins; what they apply to is the root
`.elevation-analyzers.json`. The vendored MathNetNumerics and the three test
projects are out of scope.

- `elevation` analyzes the projects a step touches, plus their dependents.
- `elevation-full` analyzes every in-scope project and judges every entry of
  `Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json`; it runs when the analyzer
  configuration, its pin or the known-findings list change, and at the end.

ELEV004 is excluded in the gate command, not in the rules. A finding recorded
in the known-findings list does not fail either gate; a new one does, and so
does a recorded one that is no longer found, so a fix removes its entry in
the same step. The list is the ledger `specs/0048/.manual/002`; it only
shrinks. Both gates require `build`: the analyzers read each project's
references as built. Set up in `specs/0048/.manual/001`.
